    "name": "central_D2_6_periodic_ast_fixture",
    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/central_D2_6_periodic: a minimal consuming model binding N=8 at the import edge (the smallest resolution the 7-point stencil admits, N >= 7). The compound match D(D(u,x),x) must fire through the section-9.6.3 fixpoint (priority 10, before any plain-D rule could lower the inner derivative) and lower to the rule's makearray — interior [4,5] holding the imported 7-point sixth-order stencil aggregate, the six near-boundary rows i in {1,2,3,6,7,8} holding the periodic-wrap 7-point differences — with all metaparameters folded and the free name dx surviving in the expanded body (the grid's consumer-supplied geometry contract). The model fulfills that contract with x0 = 0 and dx = 1/8; the dx expression is spelled with the literal 8 because the edge binding closes N before it reaches this document's scope (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm). The golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST across bindings.",
